Z||000008||mrfiero||03-02-2001||09:10 PM||||An interesting sidenote to Letterman......he used to (and maybe still does) own a Fiero!  I believe it was an '87 GT, but I'm not sure.  I do know that way back in 1991 he used that Fiero in one of his sketches.   <P>Leno seems to have an aversion to the Fiero.....he has publicly destroyed at least two of them.<P>That said, I still find myself watching Leno.....I used to be a die hard Letterman fan, but I think he lost his edge when he moved to CBS.<P>I like Craig Kilborns "5 questions"......it puts those celebs on the spot.  Conan isn't bad either.....a little on the goofy side, but still funny.||||reg||10
Z||000009||My7Fieros||03-02-2001||09:56 PM||||No question about it, Leno is top dog.<BR>Letterman is a manic depress...(litteraly), and has a piss poor attitude. Its painfully obvious to. If you pay enough attention, you can tell he dosnt even want to be there.<BR>Leno loves his job and it shows. He is also known for being a very nice and down to earth kinda guy..Ive met him before, and its true. He's very nice and personable. Letterman is funny, no doubt about it, but I like Leno much better. Besides, I think Paul Shaffer is annoying.<BR>After that, Conan beets Kilborne, hands down. Yeah hes kinda goofy, and God knows he has the absolute worst guests and music groups, but I think hes absolutly hilarious. Ive only seen Kilbornes show a few times...it was ok, but I guess that since Ive watched Conan for so long, I'll stick w/him.<BR>NBC's late night line up has got my vote over CBS's IMO.||||reg||1
Z||000010||deceler8||03-03-2001||05:35 PM||||Letterman...Irreverent humor<P>Leno...Cutting edge humor.<P>Like Conan O'Brien and Craig Kilbourn. <P>Leno has made me crap my pants so many times with OJ and Patsy Ramsey jokes that I'll probably always watch him. He shares one trait with Johnny Carson that I've always loved...their best jokes are usually the ones that make everyone groan.||||reg||1
Z||000011||fropuff||03-03-2001||11:35 PM||||I think Conan is the best!  I love Triumph the puppet dog!  I like Letterman, but I like to watch Leno for all the stuff he does on the show, such as Headlines.  If Letterman did headlines, I'd watch him instead.  I don't get good reception on CBS though.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  The thing I like about Leno is that he makes fun of himself when he knows he has a crappy joke.  ||||reg||1
